<section id="problem">
  <h2 class="mb-8 text-3xl font-bold">Why we built it</h2>
  <div class="grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-2">
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <p>Almost no film is cut by one person, and more teams work from different cities. Yet every pro editing tool treats the timeline as a one-person space.</p>
      <blockquote class="border-primary border-l-4 pl-4 italic">"It's not currently possible for more than one editor to make changes on the same timeline." <span class="not-italic opacity-70">: Adobe staff, 2017. Still true.</span></blockquote>
      <p>Writers got Google Docs. Designers got Figma. Developers got live pair programming. Film editors are still waiting for their turn.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="timeline timeline-vertical timeline-compact">
      {['Save the project file', 'Zip and upload', 'Message your partner', 'Download and relink media', 'Open it. Now they wait.'].map((s, i, a) => (
        <li>
          {i > 0 && <hr />}
          <div class="timeline-middle"><div class="badge badge-error badge-xs"></div></div>
          <div class="timeline-end timeline-box">{s}</div>
          {i < a.length - 1 && <hr />}
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
